---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const buyers = [
  ['Product / AI Product', '“Can we give this workflow more autonomy without losing a defensible action boundary?”', 'Authority Ledger + Decision Memo', 'Use the audit before adding write-capable tools, approval shortcuts or broader autonomous steps.'],
  ['Platform / Engineering', '“Do retries, object binding, external confirmation and recovery still behave coherently under failure?”', 'Evidence Contract + Finding Record', 'Use the audit when a working pilot is becoming infrastructure and operational ambiguity is getting expensive.'],
  ['Security / Assurance', '“Can we reconstruct what was authorized, what evidence existed, what changed and how uncertainty was contained?”', 'Finding Record + Decision Memo', 'Use the audit when the control question is larger than model output quality but narrower than an unbounded penetration test.'],
  ['Founder / Operations', '“What should stay autonomous, what should be constrained, and what evidence do we need before expanding?”', 'Authority Ledger + owner decision', 'Use the audit when one workflow is important enough that ownership and failure behavior need to become explicit.']
];
---

<Layout title="BitEvo — Authority Engineering Services for AI Agents" description="A decision ladder for AI-agent workflows: qualify the action chain, test one failure, audit authority and evidence, then harden verified weaknesses.">
  <section class="services-hero section">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Engineering decision ladder</div><h1 class="display">Give the workflow only the authority its evidence can support.</h1></div>
      <div><p class="lede">BitEvo engagements are organized around one progression: identify the critical action, test the uncertainty, decide how much of the <strong>Authority Budget</strong> the workflow has earned, then repair only what verified evidence supports.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/audit-intake">Map a workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-ghost" href="/diagnostic">Run the 7-gate diagnostic</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-rule">
    <div class="container service-stack">
      <article class="service panel">
        <div class="service-index">01</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Qualification</div><h2>Scope / Authority Triage</h2><p>Identify one external effect, the authority required to create it, the owner of that authority and whether a staging/test path exists. The outcome is a simple decision: audit this workflow or do not.</p><div class="chips"><span>20 minutes</span><span>1 critical action</span><span>owner identified</span><span>qualification only</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>Free</strong><small>20 min</small><a class="button" href="/audit-intake">Start with the action →</a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="service panel">
        <div class="service-index">02</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Narrow uncertainty</div><h2>Entry Audit</h2><p>Use when one suspected failure controls the decision. We test one critical action chain and one primary hypothesis to determine whether it is reproducible and decision-relevant.</p><div class="chips"><span>1 action chain</span><span>1 hypothesis</span><span>bounded reproduction</span><span>finding memo</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>$1,500</strong><small>fixed</small><a class="button" href="/audit-intake">Test the hypothesis →</a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="service primary panel">
        <div class="service-index">03</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Primary authority decision</div><h2>Agent Authority & Evidence Audit</h2><p>Use when the question is broader than one defect: has this workflow earned its current or proposed Authority Budget through sufficient evidence, independent effect confirmation and bounded recovery?</p><div class="chips"><span>5 working days</span><span>1 staging workflow</span><span>up to 3 integrations</span><span>10–20 scenarios</span><span>1 retest</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>$4,900</strong><small>fixed</small><a class="button button-primary" href="/agent-authority-audit">See the decision model →</a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="service panel">
        <div class="service-index">04</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">After verified findings</div><h2>Hardening & Repair</h2><p>Implementation is scoped only after the evidence identifies the control gap. Work is tied to explicit owner decisions, rollback requirements and retest criteria — not a generic promise to “make the agent safe.”</p><div class="chips"><span>finding-led</span><span>separate scope</span><span>rollback-aware</span><span>retest criteria</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>Quoted</strong><small>separately</small><a class="button" href="/pricing">See scope rules →</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule buyer-section">
    <div class="container buyer-head">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Owner map</div><h2 class="section-title">Same workflow. Different owner question.</h2></div>
      <p class="lede">The method stays the same, but the decision it supports changes by role. A useful engagement makes those owner questions explicit before testing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container buyer-grid">
      {buyers.map(([role, question, artifact, trigger], i) => (
        <article class="buyer panel">
          <span>{String(i + 1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>
          <div class="buyer-role">{role}</div>
          <h3>{question}</h3>
          <div class="buyer-meta"><small>PRIMARY WORK PRODUCT</small><strong>{artifact}</strong></div>
          <p>{trigger}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="container buyer-actions"><a href="/artifacts" class="button">Inspect the work products →</a><a href="/diagnostic" class="button button-ghost">Find unresolved gates</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="container principles-grid">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">What stays invariant</div><h2 class="section-title">The method does not change when the budget changes.</h2></div>
      <div class="principles">
        <article><span>01</span><div><strong>Workflow before model</strong><p>The audit object is the chain that can create an external effect: model, data, permissions, tools, approvals and recovery logic together.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><strong>Authority Budget</strong><p>Every additional write right, integration, autonomous step and retry path expands the permission surface. Capability alone does not justify that expansion.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><strong>Evidence Before Effect</strong><p>The evidence required to justify a critical action must exist at decision time. Post-hoc logs can explain an event but cannot retroactively authorize it.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><strong>External effect before “success”</strong><p>Internal completion is not proof when another system was supposed to change. Without independent confirmation, apparent success may be a False Green.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>05</span><div><strong>Owner decision before remediation</strong><p>A finding is useful only when it supports a bounded decision: expand, constrain, repair or retest. Implementation follows that decision.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="container doctrine-callout panel">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">BitEvo Doctrine</div><h2>Authority Budget · Evidence Before Effect · False Green.</h2></div>
      <div><p>These terms are not package names. They are the operating vocabulary used to describe why a workflow should gain authority, lose it, stop, recover or require stronger confirmation.</p><div class="callout-links"><a class="text-link" href="/doctrine">Open the full doctrine →</a><a class="text-link" href="/artifacts">See how doctrine becomes artifacts →</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="narrow closing">
      <div class="eyebrow">First step</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Do not describe the whole AI stack. Name the action that matters.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Start with one thing the workflow can change in the outside world. From that action we can identify the authority boundary, the evidence needed to justify it and the failure path worth testing.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/audit-intake">Map the critical action <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .services-hero{padding-top:clamp(78px,10vw,132px)}.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.12fr .88fr;gap:clamp(42px,8vw,110px);align-items:end}.hero-grid .lede{margin:0 0 24px}.hero-grid .lede strong{color:var(--ink)}.hero-actions{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}.service-stack{display:grid;gap:14px}.service{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr 170px;gap:28px;align-items:center;padding:28px 30px}.service.primary{border-color:rgba(127,208,177,.35)}.service-index{align-self:start;color:#57635f;font:500 .66rem var(--mono)}.service-copy .eyebrow{margin-bottom:8px}.service-copy h2{margin:0 0 9px;font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.5vw,1.75rem);letter-spacing:-.025em}.service-copy p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);max-width:720px}.chips{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}.chips span{padding:5px 8px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;color:#7c8986;font:500 .58rem var(--mono)}.service-side{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end}.service-side>strong{font-size:1.65rem;letter-spacing:-.04em}.service-side>small{color:var(--muted);font:500 .62rem var(--mono);margin-bottom:18px}.service-side .button{width:100%}
  .buyer-head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.78fr 1.22fr;gap:clamp(44px,8vw,110px);margin-bottom:34px}.buyer-head .lede{margin:2px 0 0}.buyer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px}.buyer{min-height:330px;padding:26px;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.buyer>span{color:#586561;font:500 .62rem var(--mono)}.buyer-role{margin-top:28px;color:var(--green);font:500 .62rem var(--mono);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.buyer h3{font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.4vw,1.7rem);line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:10px 0 24px}.buyer-meta{margin-top:auto;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}.buyer-meta small{color:var(--muted);font:500 .56rem var(--mono);letter-spacing:.1em}.buyer-meta strong{font-size:.8rem}.buyer p{margin:14px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem}.buyer-actions{display:flex;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}
  .principles-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(44px,8vw,110px)}.principles{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.principles article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:42px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.principles article>span{color:#57635f;font:500 .64rem var(--mono)}.principles strong{font-size:.9rem}.principles p{margin:5px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}.doctrine-callout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(34px,7vw,90px);padding:clamp(28px,5vw,52px);background:radial-gradient(circle at 0 0,rgba(127,208,177,.07),transparent 40%),rgba(8,16,18,.72)}.doctrine-callout h2{margin:4px 0 0;font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.7rem);letter-spacing:-.04em}.doctrine-callout p{margin:0 0 18px;color:var(--muted)}.callout-links{display:flex;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap}.text-link{font-size:.82rem;font-weight:700}.closing{text-align:center}.closing .section-title{margin-inline:auto}.closing .lede{margin:18px auto 28px}
  @media(max-width:900px){.hero-grid,.principles-grid,.doctrine-callout,.buyer-head{grid-template-columns:1fr}.service{grid-template-columns:40px 1fr}.service-side{grid-column:2;align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:row;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.service-side>small{margin:0;align-self:center}.service-side .button{width:auto;margin-left:auto}}
  @media(max-width:720px){.buyer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.buyer{min-height:280px}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.service{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:24px}.service-index{display:none}.service-side{grid-column:auto;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.service-side .button{width:100%;margin-left:0}.chips{margin-top:14px}.buyer-actions .button{width:100%}}
</style>
